      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "DanTD",
      "description": "An adopt-a-highway sign for the approaching northbound rest area along northbound Interstate 75 within the Paynes Prairie Preserve State Park in Alachua County Florida, In the spot where the person, company or organization would be posted as the sponsors of the rest area, it simply reads \"Your Name Here.\" Considering how far that sign is mounter from the road into the alligator-infested marshlands of this park, it shouldn't be that much of a surprise that nobody wants to sponsor the rest area. Or at least the FDOT doesn't want to risk the lives of any of their highway maitenance crewmembers to replace the sign.",
      "dateCreated": "2022-05-17 12:48:17",
